{"Allowing negative offsets with queryset[start_offset:stop] when enable_advanced_features=True triggers a COUNT(*) query which defeats the performance optimization purpose": 0.7345085740089417, "Redirect depth limit was reduced from 10000 to 1000 without explanation, which could silently truncate segment merges for trace trees with depth >1000": 0.9146656394004822, "Redirect depth limit should have a comment explaining the rationale and expected depth bounds": 0.3570403754711151, "Redirect depth limit should be exposed as a configurable parameter via ARGV instead of hardcoding": 0.07527033984661102, "Redirect depth limit should have metrics to track when the limit is hit": 0.1971430629491806, "1000-span hard limit uses zpopmin which evicts based on end_timestamp_precise scores, so spans with identical timestamps will be evicted in lexicographic order by payload, not FIFO": 0.7071332931518555, "1000-span limit should be configurable via ARGV to allow operational tuning without code changes": 0.026894139125943184, "1000-span limit should emit a metric when eviction occurs to track frequency and inform capacity planning": 0.16038575768470764, "The max_segment_spans check was removed creating a silent behavioral change: previously segments exceeding max_segment_spans would be logged and skipped, now they're silently capped at 1000": 0.8202189207077026, "Need to verify max_segment_spans and the Lua limit are aligned, or add a comment explaining why the check is no longer needed": 0.44010719656944275, "Negative offsets could potentially access data beyond intended boundaries if the queryset isn't properly filtered, creating authorization bypass risk": 0.4223887622356415, "The authorization check for advanced features is unclear about what security boundary it protects and should be explicitly documented": 0.07159322500228882, "If advanced features enable broader data access via negative offsets, the queryset filtering should be audited to ensure it's sufficient": 0.15274293720722198, "No backward compatibility for legacy Redis Set keys during deployment; in-flight spans could be lost if not properly drained before rollout": 0.9135642051696777, "Multiple spans with identical end_timestamp_precise values will be ordered lexicographically by payload, creating unpredictable eviction and pagination behavior that lacks test coverage": 0.4582647681236267, "Both 1000-span cap and 1000-depth redirect limit are embedded in Lua code, requiring full deployment to adjust, reducing operational flexibility": 0.031429875642061234, "Reduced redirect depth limit from 10000 to 1000 without observability metrics, risking silent behavioral changes and incomplete debugging": 0.7122079133987427}